the Triwizard Tournament is a magical  contest that is held between three of  the larger schools in the Wizarding  World Hogwarts School of Witchcraft and  Wizardry  beauxbatons academy of magic and the  durmstrang institute the location of the  tournament varies from year to year and  can be held at any of the three schools  as suggested by its name the contest  features three wizards or witches  referred to as champions each school is  represented by one champion who attempts  to complete three dangerous tasks that  have been designed to test that  champions courage intelligence  resourceful 'no sand magical ability of  course the year of 1994 was an exception  as we saw Harry take part in a contest  as not only an underage wizard but as  the fourth champion students who wish to  enter would only have to write their  names on a piece of parchment and place  that into the Goblet of Fire the Goblet  then selected the students that it  believed to be the best from each school  each student chosen will be bound by a  magical contract and had to see the  tournament through to the end the  champions received points based on their  performance these points were given up  by the Headmaster's and had mistresses  of the compete in schools who played the  role of judges the tournament was  renowned for being extremely dangerous  and over the years several champions  died while competing in the 1972  triwizard tournament all three of the  judges along with multiple students were  badly injured when a task involving a  cockatrice went wrong this led to the  tournament being discontinued after 1972  due to the high death toll the  tournament was finally revived in 1994  but this time there were restrictions  put in place to prevent the death of  those taken part all applicants now had  to be over the age of 17 to enter  but if this tournament was so dangerous  then why were there so many wizards and  witches so eager to compete there were  several rewards for those who won the  Triwizard Tournament the winner does of  course receive a prestigious Cup and as  nice as this Cup would look on a mantel  somewhere  the thought of it being a potential  portkey teleporting you to a bunch of  Death Eaters in Lord Voldemort makes  this award seem far less appealing the  winner also receives 1,000 gold galleons  but with one galleon equated to around  five muggle pounds or six or seven  dollars you won't exactly be able to  retire after winning the try was a  tournament if you're more into Fame then  as mentioned by Dumbledore himself  eternal glory  is what awaits the winner of the  Triwizard Tournament this brings us to  1994 and the most recent Triwizard  Tournament on September 1st Albus  Dumbledore announced that Hogwarts would  play host to the latest Triwizard  Tournament and on the 30th of October  the participating schools arrived at  Hogwarts the beauxbatons in a large  carriage carried by a braixen horses and  those from durmstrang in a magical ship  that could travel underwater once the  tournament and its rules had been  explained students had until the start  of the Halloween feast to enter their  names in the Goblet of Fire in order to  stop any underage wizards or witches  from entering the tournament there was  an age line drawn around the goblet of  fire the champions chosen to compete for  as follows Viktor Krum from the  durmstrang Institute Fleur Delacour  of the beauxbatons and Cedric Diggory  would be the Hogwarts champion after a  brief pause and to the surprise of  everyone the Goblet of Fire released a  fourth named Harry Potter just as Bertie  Crouch jr. planned despite the  displeasure of the other schools  Hogwarts would have two champions  representing them this year  before the tournament could commence  each champion would have to have their  ones tested to ensure that they won't  work in order the ones would be examined  by Garrick Ollivander and once satisfied  that all ones were in working order the  tournament could begin the first task  took place on the 24th of November and  each champion had to retrieve a golden  egg that was guarded by a dragon in  order to decide which dragons they'd  have to face the champions took an  intern to pull a random miniature  version of these dragons from a bag  Cedric Diggory was the first to begin  the task and would face the swedish  short snout with the use of a  Transfiguration spell he turned a  boulder into a dog in order to distract  the dragon for the most part Cedric was  successful but whilst retrieving the egg  his face was badly burnt by the dragon  despite his injuries he was still able  to complete the task Fleur Delacour was  second and made short work of the  commonwealth's green she faced by  enchanting the dragon to sleep Viktor  Krum retrieved his egg from the chinese  fireball by using a conjunctive as curse  to bind the dragon he was later deducted  points as a dragon stumbled destroying  half of the real eggs that the golden  egg was amongst last stop was harry  facing the hungarian horntail widely  regarded as the fiercest of the four  dragons using the advice given to him by  Bertie Crouch jr. who was disguised as  Professor Moody Harry summoned his broom  and outmaneuvered the dragon he did have  his shoulder slashed by the dragon  meaning he was deducted points but he  was also successful by the end of the  first task Victor and Harry were tied in  first place Cedric in second and Fleur  in third the champions were not told  what the second toss was only that the  golden egg they had retrieved contained  a clue on how to pass the second task  without deciphering the clue it would be  almost impossible to complete the second  task  after opening the egg underwater a verse  was recited and with a little help from  Moaning Myrtle  Harry worked out that the second task  involved swimming in the Black Lake the  only issue was that Harry had to figure  out a way that he could breathe  underwater for an hour Crouch jr. made  sure that never was in possession of a  book that had the answer to Harry's  dilemma and in the movie Neville does  help Harry with the use of gillyweed  however in the books that wasn't the  case Crouch jr. still disguised as  Professor moody summoned the house of  Dobby who overheard a discussion between  himself and Professor McGonagall  regarding gillyweed and the second task  wanted to help his friend Harry  they'll be stole some gillyweed from  Professor Snape's private potions store  on the morning of the task  Harry was awoken by Dobby who gave him  the gillyweed all four champions were  told that they had one hour to retrieve  something that had been stolen from them  the gillyweed gave Harry gills allowing  him to breathe underwater as well as  webbed hands and feet Cedric and Fleur  both used the bubblehead charm and  Victor transfigured himself into a shark  as the four made their way through the  village of the merpeople they discovered  that it was not an item that was taken  but a person they held dear Fleur was  forced to retire after she was attacked  by the green delouse Harry was the first  to reach the village but he was more  concerned with the safety of all the  other hostages as well as wrong Cedric  and Victor arrived shortly after  carrying away both their respective  hostages with no sign of Fleur Harry  chose to rescue both of the remaining  hostages the merpeople were tempted to  stop Harry but after a short tussle  Harry was able to break free and dragged  Ron and Fleur sister to the surface  Harry finished in third place but after  a short discussion between the judges he  was awarded second place for sure an  outstanding moral fiber Harry and Cedric  were now tied in first place with Victor  in second and flourish still in third  [Music]  the third and final task took place on  the 24th of June the task involved  navigating through a maze and reaching  the Cup located in the centre having  finished in first place Harry and Cedric  